+As for keeping this particular vulnerability undisclosed, it's not real practical.  The problem was really a pretty basic one which happens all the time.  [There may be some code running in space built against header files inappropriate for the Linux kernel installed due to problems much like this one.  Who knows?]
+I don't do almost any coding any more, but my friends who do are ga-ga over AI.  All I can say is that if AI missed a very common pre-processor issue like this, it's not very good at code checking.  Did they forget to teach the model that RNG was extra critical?  Do they even need to?  Not impressed!
